96:     - A hole is a 4-connected black component that does not touch the grid edge and is adjacent to exactly one blue object.
97: 
98:     Rule:
99:     - Leave blue pixels unchanged.
100:     - For each hole-enclosing blue object, color edge-connected black cells red when they touch that object in the 8-neighborhood.
101:     - Color black hole cells green when they touch their enclosing blue object in the 8-neighborhood.
102:     - Complete the red outline at one-cell top-left diagonal closures of the filled rim.
